# ============================================================================
# slate — environment configuration (per layer)
#
# Copy to `.env` at the repo root:   cp new.env.example .env
# `.env` is gitignored, so secrets stay out of git.
#
# WHO READS THIS FILE
#   • agent-provider (:4021)  — loads this root .env  (agents/provider/src/serve.ts)
#   • agent-consumer (:4022)  — loads this root .env  (agents/consumer/src/serve.ts)
#   • web (:3000)             — does NOT read this file. Next.js reads its own
#                               env (shell, or web/.env.local). See section 4.
#   Shell env always wins over values in this file.
#
# MOCK vs REAL (the master switch is DEPOSITOR_SECRET — section 1)
#   • DEPOSITOR_SECRET unset → OFFLINE MOCK: no chain calls, real proofs still
#     generated, settlement is mocked. Everything below can stay blank — the
#     defaults give you a working end-to-end demo with zero setup.
#   • DEPOSITOR_SECRET set   → REAL: settles on Stellar testnet. The three
#     STELLAR_*_ID contract IDs then become REQUIRED.
#
# NODE VERSION: consumer server needs Node 22+ (node:sqlite MeterDb);
# provider server needs Node 20+.
# ============================================================================


# ── 1. CHAIN / SETTLEMENT ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Read by @drongo/agent-core inside the CONSUMER process (packages/agent-core/
# src/env.ts). Governs whether settlement is mocked or real, and what it binds.

# The master switch. Funded Stellar testnet secret (S…) — the CONSUMER's
# depositor key. It funds the escrow AND submits the single settlement (the
# consumer pays for everything). Leave BLANK for offline mock mode.
# Fund a fresh keypair instantly: https://friendbot.stellar.org
DEPOSITOR_SECRET=

# Deployed Soroban contract IDs (C…). REQUIRED once DEPOSITOR_SECRET is set
# (an absent one throws a clear error); ignored in mock mode.
STELLAR_SLATE_ESCROW_ID=
STELLAR_SLATE_AGENT_REGISTRY_ID=
STELLAR_METERED_VERIFIER_ID=

# Settlement token (SEP-41 contract, C…). Defaults to native XLM's Stellar Asset
# Contract (no trustline needed; friendbot accounts work out of the box). Point
# at the USDC SAC to settle in USDC. NOTE: the provider-advertised X402_ASSET
# (section 2) overrides this for what the proof binds; this is the fallback when
# the provider advertises no asset. Whichever token is used must be whitelisted
# in the escrow (whitelist_token).
# SETTLEMENT_TOKEN_ID=
# Display label only (shown in the UI). Default: XLM.
# SETTLEMENT_TOKEN_SYMBOL=XLM

# LEGACY / normally leave BLANK. A consumer-side fallback guess of the provider's
# payout account (G…), used ONLY if the provider advertised no payTo. The current
# provider ALWAYS advertises X402_PAY_TO (section 2), so this branch is never
# taken — set the payout address there, not here. Defaults to the depositor.
# PROVIDER_PUBLIC=

# Where the durable meter / settlement state lives. Default: artifacts/metering.db
# METER_DB_PATH=artifacts/metering.db

# RPC overrides (default to Stellar testnet).
# SOROBAN_RPC_URL=https://soroban-testnet.stellar.org
# SOROBAN_NETWORK_PASSPHRASE=Test SDF Network ; September 2015


# ── 2. PROVIDER SERVER (:4021) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# The x402 resource server (agents/provider). It ADVERTISES its terms in the 402
# and meters at its own rate — the provider is the source of truth for price.

# Listen port. Default: 4021.
# ⚠ SHARED KEY: the consumer also reads PORT (as a fallback after CONSUMER_PORT).
# Leave PORT unset here and rely on the 4021 default; set CONSUMER_PORT (section
# 3) for the consumer. A bare PORT= would make BOTH servers bind the same port.
# PORT=4021

# Provider's per-unit rate in the token's DECIMAL units. Source of truth:
# advertised in the 402 and used to meter every call. Default: 0.0001.
# RATE=0.0001

# The provider's PAYOUT account (G…) — advertised in the 402 and bound into the
# proof as the settlement payee; the escrow pays exactly this address. This is
# the ONE knob that controls where funds go (PROVIDER_PUBLIC never overrides it).
# It's a PUBLIC key only: the provider never signs — the consumer's
# DEPOSITOR_SECRET pays for everything, including fees. The account only needs to
# EXIST on-network to receive (native XLM → created + min reserve; some SEP-41
# tokens → a trustline); it needs no balance for gas.
# ⚠ Set a real G… for real settlement. Default (unset) is a demo placeholder;
#   do NOT write `X402_PAY_TO=` (empty) — that advertises an empty payee, not the
#   default.
# X402_PAY_TO=G...

# SEP-41 token advertised in the 402. Default: testnet USDC.
# X402_ASSET=CBIELTK6YBZJU5UP2WWQEUCYKLPU6AUNZ2BQ4WWFEIE3USCIHMXQDAMA

# Network string in the 402. Default: stellar:testnet.
# X402_NETWORK=stellar:testnet

# Max amount (atomic units) advertised in the 402 terms. Default: 100000000.
# X402_MAX_AMOUNT=100000000

# Payment verification mode.
#   true  (default) → MockPaymentVerifier: accepts any non-empty X-PAYMENT.
#   false           → FacilitatorPaymentVerifier: POSTs to X402_FACILITATOR_URL.
# MOCK_X402=true
# External x402 facilitator (/verify + /settle) when MOCK_X402=false.
# X402_FACILITATOR_URL=http://localhost:4023


# ── 3. CONSUMER SERVER (:4022) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# The LLM-driven chat/buyer (agents/consumer). Discovers the provider's terms
# from the 402, meters per call, and settles once at shutdown.

# Listen port. Default: 4022. Use this (NOT PORT) to avoid the shared-key clash.
# CONSUMER_PORT=4022

# Which provider to open a channel with. Default: http://localhost:4021.
# PROVIDER_URL=http://localhost:4021

# Allowed browser origin for CORS (the web UI). Default: http://localhost:3000.
# CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000

# Consumer's escrow CEILING in the token's decimal units — the one price knob
# the consumer still controls. Default: 0.01.
# ESCROW=0.01

# Per-unit rate FALLBACK only. The provider-advertised RATE (section 2) wins;
# this is used solely if the provider advertised none. Default: 0.0001.
# RATE=0.0001

# x402 payment authorization presented at channel open (mock by default).
# X402_PAYMENT_SIGNATURE=

# LLM brain selection.
#   set   → OpenAiAgentBrain (real function-calling tool selection)
#   unset → StubAgentBrain (deterministic keyword router, offline, zero-cost)
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini


# ── 4. WEB UI (:3000) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Next.js front end (web). It does NOT read this root .env — set these in the
# shell or in web/.env.local. It only proxies chat to the CONSUMER server.

# Which consumer server to proxy POST /api/chat to. Default: http://localhost:4022.
# (Note: the web app talks to the consumer, not the provider.)
# AGENT_URL=http://localhost:4022
